rrowly ahead, though the newest New York Times/Siena survey gives Collins a three-point lead, and headlines remain mixed. Prediction markets price Jackson as the modest favorite, and expert raters split between Tossup and Lean D. The race sits on a knife's edge with Jackson holding a slim expected advantage.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7341, "margin": 3.16}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6906, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.626, "margin": 1.5}]}